lic tests compile.\\\",\\\"check\\\":{\\\"type\\\":\\\"command\\\",\\\"command\\\":\\\"python -m py_compile solution.py test_solution.py\\\",\\\"expected\\\":{\\\"exit_code\\\":0}}},{\\\"id\\\":\\\"SC-4\\\",\\\"description\\\":\\\"The discovered unittest suite passes.\\\",\\\"check\\\":{\\\"type\\\":\\\"command\\\",\\\"command\\\":\\\"python -m unittest discover -v\\\",\\\"expected\\\":{\\\"exit_code\\\":0}}},{\\\"id\\\":\\\"SC-5\\\",\\\"description\\\":\\\"The shared-helper refactor preserves the requested behavior, API compatibility, type hints, and input immutability while tests exercise the public API.\\\",\\\"check\\\":{\\\"type\\\":\\\"llm_judge\\\",\\\"rubric\\\":\\\"Read solution.py and test_solution.py. Determine whether both public functions delegate their shared algorithm to one private helper and retain compatible signatures, return types, imports, public names, and type hints. Assess whether the implementation visibly handles the specified key=value parsing rules and ValueError cases without mutating input collections, and whether at least two unittest methods exercise the public API. Judge only content visible in these files; do not infer test execution results.\\\"}}],\\\"verification\\\":[{\\\"command\\\":\\\"python -m py_compile solution.py test_solution.py\\\",\\\"expected\\\":{\\\"exit_code\\\":0}},{\\\"command\\\":\\\"python -m unittest discover -v\\\",\\\"expected\\\":{\\\"exit_code\\\":0}}],\\\"stop_conditions\\\":[],\\\"assumptions\\\":[\\\"Interpret the supplied task workspace as the current workspace root, and all named paths as relative to it.\\\",\\\"solution.py and test_solution.py may not exist yet and may be created or edited.\\\",\\\"Assume Python 3.11+ is available to run the requested syntax and unittest commands.\\\"]}\"}}\n{\"type\":\"turn.completed\",\"usage\":{\"input_tokens\":17425,\"cached_input_tokens\":14976,\"cache_write_input_tokens\":0,\"output_tokens\":642,\"reasoning_output_tokens\":0}}\n"}
